os_linux: don't query glibc/pthread versions on android

bionic defines neither _CS_GNU_LIBC_VERSION nor _CS_GNU_LIBPTHREAD_VERSION,
so libpthread_init() hits the "glibc too old (< 2.3.2)" #error and then four
"use of undeclared identifier '_CS_GNU_*'" errors. bionic also has no separate
pthread library to version -- it is part of libc -- so report a fixed string,
exactly as the existing MUSL_LIBC branch does.

Based on termux-packages openjdk-25 patch 0002 (Henrik Grimler), minus its
dlvsym hunk: bionic provides dlvsym from API 24 on, which their own patch 0022
walks back, and every target here builds against a higher API.

diff --git a/src/hotspot/os/linux/os_linux.cpp b/src/hotspot/os/linux/os_linux.cpp
index 7aec8b1..91c497d 100644
--- a/src/hotspot/os/linux/os_linux.cpp
+++ b/src/hotspot/os/linux/os_linux.cpp
@@ -623,6 +623,13 @@ void os::Linux::hotspot_sigmask(Thread* thread) {
 // detecting pthread library
 
 void os::Linux::libpthread_init() {
+#ifdef __ANDROID__
+  // bionic defines neither _CS_GNU_LIBC_VERSION nor _CS_GNU_LIBPTHREAD_VERSION,
+  // and its pthread implementation lives inside libc rather than a separate
+  // library, so there is no version to query. Report it like the musl case does.
+  os::Linux::set_libc_version("bionic - unknown");
+  os::Linux::set_libpthread_version("bionic - unknown");
+#else
   // Save glibc and pthread version strings.
 #if !defined(_CS_GNU_LIBC_VERSION) || \
     !defined(_CS_GNU_LIBPTHREAD_VERSION)
@@ -647,6 +654,7 @@ void os::Linux::libpthread_init() {
   confstr(_CS_GNU_LIBPTHREAD_VERSION, str, n);
   os::Linux::set_libpthread_version(str);
 #endif
+#endif
 }
 
